Here the downward current magnetizes every part of the wire
 in a tangential direction, as indicated by the letters $N S$.


The twisting of the wire in the direction of a right-handed
 screw causes the portion $A B C D$ to be extended along the
 diagonal $A C$ and compressed along the diagonal $B D$. The
 direction of magnetization therefore tends to approach $A C$ and
 to recede from $B D$, and thus the lower end becomes a north pole
 and the upper end a south pole.


